Subject: Adapt original event ownership, delivery and registry lifetime

Upstream-base: 2c71062ca827c5d2115ab76f4da80aaa8c515ff8

Keep original event hashing, AVL registration, listener ordering and callback
transfer. Native owners retain full addresses; flags/counts use explicit masks
and listeners keep typed entry back-pointers. Defer removals during delivery,
validate type lookup and registration, and initialize/shut down after/before
game arenas. Native connection trees use existing game-owned NewAdapter nodes;
bounded scope barriers require scoped listeners to be disconnected before pop,
then reclaim empty groups without restoring stale pooled AVL nodes. Unselected
Wii paths retain their original pool-state code. Consume callback storage through
mutable native members and transfer the active union member. Extract the
three-argument template from controller headers so it can be built independently
of Wii input services. Queued dispatch and game task globals remain unselected.
Runtime support is in src/.

